    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice if the `MiniSessions.config.hooks.pre.read` were able to abort loading a session based on the data they receive from `MiniSessions.detected` by returning `false`.\n\nSo calling \n```lua\nMiniSessions.read(nil, { \n  hooks = { \n    pre = function(session) return session.type == 'local' end\n  }\n})\n````\n would only load a local session if one was available and do nothing otherwise.\n\n\n**Why this would be needed:** Not being able to do this is an issue when using the default `Snacks.picker.projects()` or `Snacks.picker.zoxide()` from [snacks.nvim](https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim) because it can not tell mini.sessions to only load a local session if available and thus just loads the last session if any folder is selected in the picker.\n\nSnacks.nvim currently can only call `MiniSessions.read()`:\nhttps://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim/blob/bc0630e43be5699bb94dadc302c0d21615421d93/lua/snacks/dashboard.lua#L832-L833\n\nChanging the 'pre' hook in the `read()` function to stop the loading if the 'pre' hook returns false:\nFrom:\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/efff26174ca363c059f92e906753db47e81d870b/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L195-L196\nTo:\n```lua\nif H.possibly_execute(opts.hooks.pre, data) == false the\n  return\nend\n```\n\nWould allow for snacks.nvim to use:\n```lua\n{ \"mini.sessions\", \":lua require('mini.sessions').read(nil, { hooks = { pre = function(session) return session.type == 'local' end } })\" },\n{ \"mini.nvim\", \":lua require('mini.sessions').read(nil, { hooks = { pre = function(session) return session.type == 'local' end } })\" },\n```\n\nWhich would fix the integration with mini.sessions when using the Snacks picker.\n\nI'd be happy to make a PR, if this is a desired functionality.",
