        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough it looks reasonable, it would require establishing a pattern for all (at least `pre`) hooks, which I am not really a fan of.\n\nThe value of these entries was a [deliberate decision](https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim/issues/144#issuecomment-2494404092) to leverage the default behavior of `read()`: source local if present, fall back to latest.\n\n> ...because it can not tell mini.sessions to only load a local session if available and thus just loads the last session if any folder is selected in the picker.\n\nThis can be done via something like this: `:lua if MiniSessions == nil then require('mini.sessions').setup() end; pcall(MiniSessions.read, MiniSessions.config.file)`. I.e. ensure sessions are detected and try reading a local session.\n\nI'll think about it a bit more, but I am hesitant at the moment about this (especially since there is a solution for the original problem).",
